{"duration": 57.981, "exact_word_timing": true, "lines": [{"beat": 0, "text": "A priest steadies a handful of tiny ceramic spoons over a fresh burial.", "start": 0.08, "end": 3.993}, {"beat": 0, "text": "The clay cups glint like tiny moons in the dim light.", "start": 4.213, "end": 6.962}, {"beat": 0, "text": "He whispers that each spoon carries a secret for the dead.", "start": 7.182, "end": 9.777}, {"beat": 1, "text": "His apprentices laugh, saying the dead don\u2019t need kitchen tools.", "start": 10.197, "end": 13.421}, {"beat": 1, "text": "One scoffs, \"What will a ghost eat?\"", "start": 13.641, "end": 15.372}, {"beat": 1, "text": "Another rolls his eyes, shaking his head.", "start": 15.592, "end": 17.657}, {"beat": 2, "text": "The priest places each spoon beside the skull, the clay cool against the earth.", "start": 18.077, "end": 21.788}, {"beat": 2, "text": "He slides a red powder into every tiny bowl.", "start": 22.008, "end": 24.451}, {"beat": 2, "text": "The air smells faintly of metal and incense.", "start": 24.671, "end": 26.956}, {"beat": 3, "text": "You see how you tuck a favorite trinket into a loved one\u2019s pocket for comfort.", "start": 27.376, "end": 31.3}, {"beat": 3, "text": "It feels like a promise that something familiar travels with them.", "start": 31.52, "end": 34.59}, {"beat": 4, "text": "The real reason: the spoons held cinnabar, a bright red mercury sulfide.", "start": 35.01, "end": 39.248}, {"beat": 4, "text": "Cinnabar was used in Maya funerary rites to feed the spirit\u2019s journey.", "start": 39.468, "end": 43.386}, {"beat": 4, "text": "Its vivid colour symbolized blood, life, and the after\u2011world.", "start": 43.606, "end": 47.054}, {"beat": 5, "text": "Because cinnabar is toxic, those tiny spoons turned every grave into a silent, centuries\u2011long warning.", "start": 47.474, "end": 53.623}, {"beat": 5, "text": "Even centuries later, the poison still lingers in the soil.", "start": 53.843, "end": 56.861}], "words": [{"w": 